# Rust
/rust-core/target/
# Cargo.lock deliberately NOT ignored (fixed -- it was, wrongly): rust-core builds directly
# into the Android app, an application deliverable, not a library published for other crates
# to depend on. Committing the lockfile pins exact transitive versions (including ct-common's
# git+tag dependency and every crypto crate under it) for reproducible builds across CI, other
# machines, and time -- the usual reason libraries exclude it doesn't apply here.

# Android / Gradle
/android/.gradle/
/android/build/
/android/app/build/
/android/local.properties
# rust-core/build/ specifically -- missed initially, caught the hard way: `git add -A`
# staged the *entire* generated Gradle build output (compiled .class files, the .aar,
# copied .so libs, Kotlin incremental-compile caches) because only android/build/ was
# listed, not rust-core/build/ (a sibling Gradle module outside android/).
/rust-core/build/
*.iml
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
